The CUDA kernel `timedReduction` in main.cu is adapted from:

    NVIDIA/cuda-samples, cpp/0_Introduction/clock/clock.cu
    https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-samples/blob/master/cpp/0_Introduction/clock/clock.cu
    Copyright (c) 2022, NVIDIA CORPORATION. All rights reserved.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: (BSD-3-Clause)

Only the `clock_t *timer` parameter and the two `clock()` timestamp
calls (and the `__syncthreads()` that existed solely to make the
trailing timestamp include all reduction work) were removed, since that
instrumentation is diagnostic-only and irrelevant to a deterministic
output comparison; the dynamic-shared-memory tree-halving reduction
algorithm itself is otherwise unmodified from the upstream file.

